# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the sanitized engine (scripts/build-sanitized.sh, CI's sanitizers.yml).
# Only leaks unmodified chdman 0.289 has too belong here, each with how that was checked.
#
# MAME's work queue (src/osd/osdsync.cpp, unchanged in engine/) loses some of the work items the
# compressor queues from its read thread, and the events waiting on them creates, and frees them only
# at exit: a few dozen bytes per hunk. chdman 0.289 built from the MAME release with
# -fsanitize=address reports the same leak on every run of
#   createdvd -i agent.iso -o x.chd -f -np 1 -c zlib,huff
# (checked 2026-10-02). The page's compression doesn't queue its hunks there (helper workers do it).
leak:osd_work_item_queue_multiple
leak:osd_work_item_wait
